WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:05.369
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.369 --> 00:00:12.542
How many of you have ever made a big
life decision solely based on logic?

00:00:12.542 --> 00:00:14.314
Quite a few of you.

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:18.305
Well, can you imagine
turning down your dream job,

00:00:18.305 --> 00:00:22.397
moving across the country and
applying to Stanford.

00:00:22.397 --> 00:00:23.967
All because your body said so.

00:00:23.967 --> 00:00:27.128
Well, that's what I did.

00:00:27.128 --> 00:00:32.005
You see, a few years ago,
I made a discovery about my intuition,

00:00:32.005 --> 00:00:36.706
what I now call body wisdom that
has profoundly changed the way I

00:00:36.706 --> 00:00:41.516
think about the world and
make every single decisionin my life.

00:00:41.516 --> 00:00:44.853
Intuition is a hot topic,
a quick Google search and

00:00:44.853 --> 00:00:49.985
you will find thousands of articles on
mindful hitting and trusting your gut.

00:00:49.985 --> 00:00:53.489
But my intuition started
a really long time ago.

00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:58.661
It started when I was ten years old.

00:00:58.661 --> 00:01:04.127
I remember staring at
this quarter in a jar.

00:01:04.127 --> 00:01:09.465
If it lands on heads, I'll tell

00:01:09.465 --> 00:01:14.413
them please don't be heads.

00:01:14.413 --> 00:01:17.763
Heads, two to three.

00:01:17.763 --> 00:01:24.867
Don't be heads come on,
don't be heads Heads,

00:01:24.867 --> 00:01:30.133
I flipped this coin more than 10
times until I finally mustered

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:35.020
up the courage to slit a note
underneath my family's door.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:39.610
Mom, Dad,
I'm gay my body immediately opens up like

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:43.793
an exhale after attempting
to hold your breath.

00:01:43.793 --> 00:01:46.751
I felt warm and grounded, free.

00:01:46.751 --> 00:01:49.244
And my parents did as many would do,

00:01:49.244 --> 00:01:52.747
suggest that I wait until I was older,
to be sure.

00:01:52.747 --> 00:01:54.172
And that's what I did.

00:01:54.172 --> 00:01:59.040
The next day in social studies class,
I blocked that night from my mind.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.877
And it worked for eight years,
I'd remain closeted.

00:02:02.877 --> 00:02:07.638
And I would channel this energy into my
personal computer and building websites.

00:02:07.638 --> 00:02:12.659
Tech became my outlet,
the perfect distraction,

00:02:12.659 --> 00:02:15.353
until I was 18 years old.

00:02:15.353 --> 00:02:19.230
Hey Mom and Dad remember that note
I wrote you like eight years ago?

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:23.391
Turns out big surprise I am gay.

00:02:23.391 --> 00:02:28.521
But what did I forget all those years,
those eight long years.

00:02:28.521 --> 00:02:33.305
For a long time, I thought I simply
forgot my sexual orientation.

00:02:33.305 --> 00:02:35.491
But it's bigger than that.

00:02:35.491 --> 00:02:40.835
What I see now that I have forgotten
was my intuition, my body wisdom,

00:02:40.835 --> 00:02:46.829
the part of me the part of all of us that
knows exactly who we are and what we need.

00:02:46.829 --> 00:02:47.697
So what is body wisdom?

00:02:47.697 --> 00:02:49.355
Let's define it.

00:02:49.355 --> 00:02:52.265
Body wisdom are the signals
your body gives you

00:02:52.265 --> 00:02:56.605
when he either needs something from you or
when you ask it a question.

00:02:56.605 --> 00:02:59.808
When your stomach grouse, what do we do?

00:02:59.808 --> 00:03:04.419
We eat, when we yawn, we sleep.

00:03:04.419 --> 00:03:08.654
These are all moments our
bodies communicate with us, and

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:12.898
thank God we listen, or
else we'd be hungry all the time.

00:03:12.898 --> 00:03:16.325
So, can you imagine if you
could trust your body,

00:03:16.325 --> 00:03:21.235
just like when your stomach grouse
in the face of a difficult decision.

00:03:21.235 --> 00:03:26.794
.We'd have less anxiety, less decision
fatigue and maybe even less regret.

00:03:26.794 --> 00:03:31.937
I call this the body wisdom cycle and
it's a very simple idea.

00:03:31.937 --> 00:03:36.760
First, your body communicates with
you in the face of a decision.

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:41.586
You then make a choice and listen to your
body that's aligned with what it's saying.

00:03:41.586 --> 00:03:46.173
Then third, you signal back to your brain,
I trust myself.

00:03:46.173 --> 00:03:49.598
Because if you trust your body,
you trust yourself and

00:03:49.598 --> 00:03:52.066
if you trust yourself, you're free.

00:03:52.066 --> 00:03:55.897
And what if I was to tell you that
this is actually rooted in science?

00:03:55.897 --> 00:04:00.533
Neurological research shows that patients
who damage the limbic system part of

00:04:00.533 --> 00:04:05.042
their brain, which is the oldest part,
are incapable of making decisions.

00:04:05.042 --> 00:04:07.276
Interestingly, their logic is fine.

00:04:07.276 --> 00:04:09.929
Their language abilities are fine.

00:04:09.929 --> 00:04:13.887
But it's their emotions that
they have trouble accessing.

00:04:13.887 --> 00:04:18.038
In other words, we need emotions
to make decisions in our lives.

00:04:18.038 --> 00:04:21.121
And how do emotions reveal themselves?

00:04:21.121 --> 00:04:23.915
Through our heart, our bodies our breath.

00:04:23.915 --> 00:04:29.473
That is why body wisdom is so
critical for decision making.

00:04:29.473 --> 00:04:35.313
I want to take you back to that ten year
old version of me who just came out to his

00:04:35.313 --> 00:04:42.000
family within six months, I developed OCD,
a type of anxiety that felt really scary.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:45.801
I would feel paralyzed in
the face of a decision.

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:50.070
In this type of anxiety came full
circle when I entered my 20s.

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:55.161
I was studying abroad in Paris,
and I fell in love with the city.

00:04:55.161 --> 00:05:00.301
It was my dream, my mission to work and
live there someday.

00:05:00.301 --> 00:05:05.231
After years of French tutoring and
multiple phone screenings I found

00:05:05.231 --> 00:05:08.806
myself on a flight to interview for
a job in Paris.

00:05:08.806 --> 00:05:14.246
I remember speaking for hours in French
during the interview, it felt magical.

00:05:14.246 --> 00:05:21.792
And then HR called [FOREIGN].

00:05:21.792 --> 00:05:25.608
I got the job I felt victorious and

00:05:25.608 --> 00:05:31.885
then suddenly unexpectedly,
fell torn up in my body.

00:05:31.885 --> 00:05:34.638
Because while I had
been practicing French,

00:05:34.638 --> 00:05:38.851
I'd also been rediscovering my
childhood passion for technology.

00:05:38.851 --> 00:05:41.592
I taught myself how to build mobile apps,
and

00:05:41.592 --> 00:05:44.848
I was about to launch my first
app on the IOS App Store.

00:05:44.848 --> 00:05:49.436
And I was afraid saying yes to Paris,
would mean to turn my app launch, and

00:05:49.436 --> 00:05:51.002
long term career goals.

00:05:51.002 --> 00:05:54.159
I was at a fork in the road,
but this time,

00:05:54.159 --> 00:05:57.784
I didn't have a coin to
help me make a decision.

00:05:57.784 --> 00:06:02.318
And this lack of direction reminded
me of being ten years old.

00:06:02.318 --> 00:06:09.468
So at that moment, I started to listen
to my body my lungs felt constricted and

00:06:09.468 --> 00:06:13.434
narrow and tight my stomach felt twisted.

00:06:13.434 --> 00:06:16.548
I was so cold I was shivering.

00:06:16.548 --> 00:06:19.023
But should I listen to my body?

00:06:19.023 --> 00:06:21.521
The logical part of my brain it made so
much more sense.

00:06:21.521 --> 00:06:23.784
This was my dream job.

00:06:23.784 --> 00:06:27.356
What am I supposed to do?

00:06:27.356 --> 00:06:30.301
It was at that moment
that I had an epiphany.

00:06:30.301 --> 00:06:35.131
I realized if I could listen to my
body wisdom in this moment regret is

00:06:35.131 --> 00:06:36.158
impossible.

00:06:36.158 --> 00:06:39.378
Because if we trust our bodies,
we trust ourselves and

00:06:39.378 --> 00:06:41.626
if we trust ourselves, we're free.

00:06:41.626 --> 00:06:43.573
When I was younger,
my intuition came to be.

00:06:43.573 --> 00:06:47.939
And in this moment,
I realized my body could be at war.

00:06:47.939 --> 00:06:50.505
To ease my anxiety around decision making.

00:06:52.512 --> 00:06:55.121
So I said no to Paris.

00:06:55.121 --> 00:06:57.543
I stayed in New York.

00:06:57.543 --> 00:06:59.429
My app trended on the App Store.

00:06:59.429 --> 00:07:04.412
And now I'm here at Stanford,
where I absolutely want to be.

00:07:04.412 --> 00:07:09.093
And I have made every decision
since with my body and mind.

00:07:09.093 --> 00:07:13.065
Now could I see a world
where I'm not at Stanford,

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:17.711
I'm in Paris, sipping espresso and
eating croissants?

00:07:17.711 --> 00:07:22.455
Of course, trusting your body
does not mean you don't get to

00:07:22.455 --> 00:07:24.791
look back on paths not taken.

00:07:24.791 --> 00:07:29.737
It simply means you trust your body
knew what you needed at a point in time.

00:07:29.737 --> 00:07:33.520
It just wasn't using
words to tell you why.

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:39.969
Because to try and exercise together
want everyone to close their eyes.

00:07:39.969 --> 00:07:43.892
Picture in your mind
a decision you have to make.

00:07:43.892 --> 00:07:49.238
This decision could be need to make
today tomorrow, maybe a year from now.

00:07:49.238 --> 00:07:51.808
It could be small like what to eat for
dinner?

00:07:51.808 --> 00:07:53.879
Or maybe it's bigger.

00:07:53.879 --> 00:07:57.573
A fork in the road that
could change your life.

00:07:57.573 --> 00:08:02.229
Now see yourself making that decision
in your mind, go through with it.

00:08:02.229 --> 00:08:06.324
Don't feel too committed to it,
it's just an exercise.

00:08:06.324 --> 00:08:11.673
Now notice what's around you in your mind,
and feel your body,

00:08:11.673 --> 00:08:15.745
could put your hand on
your chest if you'd like.

00:08:15.745 --> 00:08:19.770
Your lungs may feel airy and open.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:22.990
Your stomach maybe feels really settled.

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:26.332
Your temperature may be slightly warm,

00:08:26.332 --> 00:08:31.747
a little tingly soft means your
body is aligned with this choice.

00:08:31.747 --> 00:08:35.869
You may also feel other types
of sensations in your body.

00:08:35.869 --> 00:08:40.095
Your lungs may feel constricted and
tighter,

00:08:40.095 --> 00:08:44.765
your stomach may feel twisted,
you may feel cold.

00:08:44.765 --> 00:08:49.294
This doesn't have to mean your decision is
wrong just may mean your body is trying to

00:08:49.294 --> 00:08:50.467
tell you something.

00:08:50.467 --> 00:08:54.863
And that may be something
worth listening to.

00:08:54.863 --> 00:08:58.569
Everyone can open their eyes now.

00:08:58.569 --> 00:09:02.668
That is body wisdom.

00:09:02.668 --> 00:09:05.580
Now this practice is a practice.

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:08.010
It's not easy to listen to your body.

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:12.491
It's something I practice every day but
if you try it,

00:09:12.491 --> 00:09:16.203
I think you'll be amazed what you'll find.

00:09:16.203 --> 00:09:21.612
There's so much in this world
that causes us all anxiety.

00:09:21.612 --> 00:09:24.215
I hope by following this practice,

00:09:24.215 --> 00:09:29.694
you have one more tool at your disposal,
and one less thing to worry about.

00:09:29.694 --> 00:09:36.770
But as with all decisions A choice to
trust your body is yours, thank you.

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:38.303
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:09:38.303 --> 00:09:42.286
[MUSIC]

